e had said goodbye to his colleagues, his voice steady, his eyes calm, masking the unease that had begun to creep into his thoughts. The final briefing had been brief, a list of protocols and warnings, followed by the command to proceed. He had walked to the airlock, the heavy doors closing behind him with a finality that echoed in his bones, marking the beginning of his solitary vigil."
